.TH "GF-QUOTA-UPDATE-USER-QUOTA" "1" "May 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-quota-update-user-quota - Updates user quota


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf quota update-user-quota [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Updates user quota

.PP
If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled, you need to have a permission with action \fBusers.quotas:update\fR and scope \fBglobal.users:1\fR (userIDScope).

.PP
Body schema (UpdateQuotaCmd):
{
  "limit": number,
  "target": string
}


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	Request body JSON or path to a JSON file (e.g. --body=/path/to/body.json, --body='{"foo": "bar"}'). The 'Body schema' block is a type reference; use --describe-body-jsonschema for a strict JSON Schema.

.PP
\fB--describe-body-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the request body and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB--describe-response-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the response payload and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update-user-quota

.PP
\fB--quota-target\fP=""
	QuotaTarget

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	Print the raw HTTP response body instead of the decoded payload

.PP
\fB--user-id\fP=0
	UserID


